# Storybook — AWT UI System Documentation

Document the first-party design system so Storybook is the source of truth for `apps/web` UI. Align with skills `awt-dashboard-ui`, `ux-writing`, `dashboard-ui-review`, and `dashboard-ui-prototyping`.

## Placement and naming

- Colocate stories next to the component: `ComponentName.stories.tsx` beside `ComponentName.tsx`
- **Components** = kit reutilizable (primitives + app chrome + domain blocks)
- **Pages** = decisiones de diseño del producto (flujos compuestos, brand en contexto)
- Kit primitives on disk: `apps/web/src/shared/components/UI/**`
- Composites on disk: `Global/`, `sections/`, `preferences/` under `shared/components/`
- Product flows on disk: `auth/presentation/**/*.stories.tsx`, `shared/components/brand/**`
- Title hierarchy (must match `storySort` in `preview.tsx`):

```
Design System/Introducción
Design System/Components/UI/<Component>
Design System/Components/Global/<Name>
Design System/Components/Sections/<Name>
Design System/Components/Preferences/<Name>
Design System/Pages/Auth/<Name>
Design System/Pages/Brand/<Name>
```

- Folder on disk: kebab-case (`text-field/`). Story `title` segment: PascalCase component name
- Export `index.ts` for every kit component; stories import from the local file or barrel consistently with neighbors

## CSF3 meta (required)

```tsx
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/react-vite'
import { Component } from './Component'

const meta = {
  title: 'Design System/Components/UI/Component',
  component: Component,
  tags: ['autodocs'],
  parameters: {
    layout: 'centered', // use 'padded' or 'fullscreen' for layout-heavy / shell components
    controls: { expanded: true },
  },
  argTypes: {
    // document every public visual prop with control + description
  },
} satisfies Meta<typeof Component>

export default meta
type Story = StoryObj<typeof meta>
```

Rules:

- Prefer `satisfies Meta<typeof Component>` over loose `Meta`
- `tags: ['autodocs']` on all kit primitives
- Describe `argTypes` for variants, sizes, booleans, and slots — Controls + Docs become the API card
- Do not hide important props from Controls unless they are callbacks (then `action` / disable control)
- Default `args` must render a valid, accessible happy path

## Story catalog (minimum set)

Every kit component documents these stories when the state exists in the API:

| Story | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `Default` / `Playground` | Happy path + full Controls |
| Variant matrix | One story or grouped stories per `variant` / `size` |
| `Loading` | Spinner/skeleton — panel-scoped, not fake full-app block |
| `Empty` | Use kit `Empty` patterns; CTA copy via `ux-writing` |
| `Error` / disabled / invalid | Failure and non-interactive states |
| `Dense` / long content | Truncation, wrap, overflow (lived-in data) |
| Icon-only / a11y edge | Prove `aria-label` and keyboard focus |

Prototyping divergent layouts: follow `dashboard-ui-prototyping` — named stories (`Ops Dense`, `Master Detail`), then remix; do not leave abandoned WIP stories without `.wip` in the filename or explicit removal.

## Design-system construction (from `awt-dashboard-ui`)

- Stories must use theme tokens / Tailwind theme classes — no hard-coded hex in story JSX
- Compose only existing kit primitives inside composite stories; do not invent one-off controls in Storybook that do not exist in `UI/`
- Responsive: for layout components, add `parameters.viewport` or fullscreen stories at narrow width; flag horizontal overflow as a defect (`dashboard-ui-review`)

## Light / dark mode (required)

Wired in `.storybook/preview.tsx` + `decorators.tsx`:

- Toolbar **Tema** → `globals.theme` (`light` | `dark`)
- `withThemeClass` sets `document.documentElement` class + `data-theme`
- `withPreferences` wraps `ThemeProvider` / `LocaleProvider` / `UiPreferencesProvider`
- Global `backgrounds` disabled — surface comes from theme tokens, not Storybook bg picker

Rules:

- Components and stories use semantic tokens (`surface-*`, `text-*`, `brand-*`, borders) from `theme.css` — never `#fff` / `#000` / hard light-only greys
- Verify every new story in **both** toolbar themes before merge (contrast, borders, hover, focus rings)
- Dedicated `Dark` story only when behavior/layout diverges from light; otherwise toolbar is enough
- Do not override root theme with local `className="dark"` / forced light wrappers inside stories
- Charts/images/brand assets: check legibility on dark surfaces; invert or swap asset if needed
- Fail review if a control disappears or loses contrast in one theme (`dashboard-ui-review`)

## i18n / translations (required)

Wired in `.storybook/i18n.ts` + toolbar **Idioma** (`es` | `en`):

- `withLocale` syncs `i18next.changeLanguage` + `lang` on `<html>`
- Resources: `@/shared/i18n/resources` plus Storybook extras in `.storybook/i18n.ts`

Rules:

- **Production components** that show UI copy use `useTranslation` / `t('key')` — no hard-coded user-facing Spanish/English in component source
- Stories for i18n-aware components: render via `t()` or mount the real component so toolbar locale switches text; do not bake only one language into `args` when the component is translated
- Stories for dumb/presentational props that take `title` / `label` strings: literals in `args` OK; document that product screens must pass translated strings
- New Storybook-only demo strings (nav fixtures, etc.): add **both** `es` and `en` under `.storybook/i18n.ts` extras — never Spanish-only extras
- New app strings: add keys to shared i18n resources for **es** and **en** in the same PR as the UI
- Verify primary stories with toolbar `es` and `en` (truncation, layout grow, RTL not required unless product asks)
- Empty/error CTA copy: follow `ux-writing`; keys must exist in both locales
- `aria-label` and `title` tooltips that are user-facing follow the same i18n rules as visible text

## Docs quality

- Autodocs + meaningful prop `description`s; JSDoc on exported props interfaces so Docs picks them up
- MDX only for overview / principles (`Introducción`), not for duplicating every prop table
- One job per story: avoid mega-stories that bury the prop under review
- Sample data: realistic and messy (long names, empty fields, many rows) — not `lorem` / `foo`
- Actions: wire `onClick` / `onChange` with Storybook actions when useful for verification

## Accessibility in Storybook

- Addon a11y is enabled — fix violations before merging UI stories
- Icon-only controls in stories must include accessible names
- Do not disable a11y checks to “pass” CI; fix the component
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` in any demo animation

## Anti-patterns

- Stories outside the `Design System/...` title tree for kit components
- Snapshot-only stories with no Controls for public props
- Duplicating production pages in **Components** instead of **Pages/Auth** (or the relevant Pages group)
- Hard-coded light-only backgrounds that fight the theme decorator (`backgrounds: { disable: true }` is global — do not reintroduce conflicting backgrounds)
- Hex colors or light-only greys that break in dark mode
- Hard-coded UI strings in kit components that should go through i18n
- Storybook extras / keys present in only one locale (`es` without `en` or reverse)
- Shipping new `UI/` components without a colocated `*.stories.tsx`
- Parallel “demo components” living only in Storybook

## Checklist before merge

- [ ] Colocated `*.stories.tsx` with correct `title`
- [ ] `autodocs` + documented `argTypes`
- [ ] Default + key variants + loading/empty/error when applicable
- [ ] Toolbar **Tema**: light + dark OK (contrast, borders, focus)
- [ ] Toolbar **Idioma**: `es` + `en` OK (copy, truncation, layout)
- [ ] New strings in shared i18n (or SB extras) for both locales
- [ ] a11y clean on primary stories
- [ ] Tokens only; reuses kit; matches `awt-dashboard-ui`
- [ ] Copy on empty/error CTAs reviewed with `ux-writing` when user-facing

